%% Seeding and catch-up options plotted against link dependence and cutover downtime - Contoso profile
%% Source: Microsoft Learn "Migration overview for SMB Azure file shares" (tool table and fidelity column), "Migrate data into Azure File Sync with Azure Data Box" (offline bulk seed then zero-downtime catch-up), "Introduction to Azure Storage Mover" (Data Box plus Mover online catch-up, metadata-only uploads), "Migrate to Azure Files using RoboCopy" (downtime equals the last pass)
quadrantChart
  title Where each option sits - x is how much of the seed must cross the ExpressRoute link, y is how long the department is offline at cutover
  x-axis "Whole seed crosses the wire" --> "Bulk seed travels offline"
  y-axis "Downtime measured in hours" --> "Downtime close to zero"
  quadrant-1 "Offline seed and a near-zero cutover - the default for large Contoso shares"
  quadrant-2 "Wire seed and a near-zero cutover - the default for shares the link can carry"
  quadrant-3 "Wire seed with a real outage - only for small or archival shares"
  quadrant-4 "Offline seed but still a real outage - accept only when no catch-up tool fits the source"
  Azure File Sync direct upload: [0.14, 0.92]
